---
import GuideLayout from "@/layouts/GuideLayout.astro";
import { SITE_URL } from "@/lib/seo";
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildArticleSchema } from "@/lib/schema";

const title = "JWT Decoder Workflow — Complete Guide | ToolBite";
const description = "Decode JWT tokens safely for debugging: inspect headers and payloads, check exp, iss and aud claims, and understand why decode is not verification.";
const canonicalPath = "/guides/jwt-decoder-guide.html";
const pageUrl = `${SITE_URL}${canonicalPath}`;
const schemas = [
  buildArticleSchema({ title, description, url: pageUrl }),
  buildBreadcrumbSchema([
    { name: "Home", url: SITE_URL },
    { name: "Guides", url: `${SITE_URL}/guides.html` },
    { name: "JWT Decoder Guide", url: pageUrl }
  ])
];
---

<GuideLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
  schemas={schemas}
  badge="Security"
  badgeColor="#f87171"
  icon="🪪"
  readTime="5 min read"
>
  <article class="gl-article">

    <div class="gl-box gl-box--warn">
      <span class="gl-box-icon">⚠️</span>
      <span><strong>Important:</strong> this guide is about local inspection for debugging. Decoding is not the same as signature verification — never grant access based on a decoded payload alone.</span>
    </div>

    <h2>What is a JWT?</h2>
    <p>A JSON Web Token (JWT) has three Base64url-encoded segments separated by dots: <code>header.payload.signature</code>. The header declares the algorithm, the payload holds claims (user ID, expiry, roles), and the signature proves the token was issued by a trusted party.</p>
    <p>Decoding reads the first two segments. Verifying checks the signature against a secret or public key — that's the step that determines whether to trust the token.</p>

    <h2>Safe debugging workflow</h2>
    <ol class="gl-steps">
      <li>Open <a href="/tools/jwt-decoder.html">ToolBite's JWT Decoder</a> — it runs locally, your token never leaves the browser.</li>
      <li>Paste the token and inspect the header: check <code>alg</code> and <code>kid</code>.</li>
      <li>Read the payload claims listed below.</li>
      <li>Verify the signature server-side before using any claim to authorize a request.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Key claims to inspect</h2>
    <div class="gl-quick-ref">
      <h3>Payload claims reference</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>exp</strong> — expiry timestamp (Unix epoch). Token is invalid after this time.</li>
        <li><strong>nbf</strong> — not-before. Token is invalid before this time.</li>
        <li><strong>iat</strong> — issued-at. When the token was created.</li>
        <li><strong>iss</strong> — issuer. Must match your expected auth provider.</li>
        <li><strong>aud</strong> — audience. Must match your app's identifier.</li>
        <li><strong>sub</strong> — subject. Usually the user ID.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Common mistakes to avoid</h2>
    <ul class="gl-checklist">
      <li><strong>Trusting decoded data without verification</strong> — the payload can be forged if the signature is not validated.</li>
      <li><strong>Ignoring clock skew</strong> — clocks between servers drift. Allow a small buffer (60s) when checking <code>exp</code> and <code>nbf</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Not validating <code>iss</code> and <code>aud</code></strong> — a token from one app could be replayed in another if you skip audience checks.</li>
      <li><strong>Using <code>alg: none</code></strong> — always reject tokens with no algorithm. Libraries should do this by default; verify yours does.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Safer team workflow</h2>
    <p>Decode locally in the browser for quick debugging. Redact sensitive samples before pasting into tickets or Slack. Keep verification logic in code-reviewable backend services — never move signature checking to the client.</p>

    <div class="gl-box gl-box--success">
      <span class="gl-box-icon">✅</span>
      <span>Browser-based decoders like ToolBite are good for inspecting tokens during development because nothing is sent to a server. Never paste production tokens into third-party online tools you don't control.</span>
    </div>

    <h2>JWT review checklist</h2>
    <ul class="gl-checklist">
      <li>Token is meant for the correct environment and application.</li>
      <li><code>exp</code>, <code>nbf</code>, and <code>iat</code> align with your session rules.</li>
      <li><code>iss</code> and <code>aud</code> are verified server-side before using the token.</li>
      <li>Custom role or permission claims are not trusted until signature validation passes.</li>
      <li>Algorithm is not <code>none</code>.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="gl-cta-row">
      <a href="/tools/jwt-decoder.html" class="tb-btn tb-btn-primary">Open JWT Decoder →</a>
      <a href="/guides/base64-encoding-guide.html" class="tb-btn tb-btn-outline">Base64 guide</a>
      <a href="/tools/json-formatter.html" class="tb-btn tb-btn-outline">Format decoded JSON</a>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section>
    <p class="gl-section-heading">Tools used in this guide</p>
    <div class="gl-tools-row">
      <a href="/tools/jwt-decoder.html" class="gl-tool-btn"><span aria-hidden="true">🪪</span> JWT Decoder</a>
      <a href="/tools/json-formatter.html" class="gl-tool-btn"><span aria-hidden="true">💻</span> JSON Formatter</a>
      <a href="/tools/base64-encoder.html" class="gl-tool-btn"><span aria-hidden="true">📎</span> Base64 Encoder</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="gl-section-heading">Related guides & tools</p>
    <div class="gl-related">
      <a href="/guides/base64-encoding-guide.html" class="gl-card">
        <span class="gl-card-icon">📎</span>
        <p class="gl-card-title">Base64 Encoding</p>
        <p class="gl-card-desc">JWT uses Base64url — understand the encoding underneath.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/guides/hash-functions-explained.html" class="gl-card">
        <span class="gl-card-icon">🔢</span>
        <p class="gl-card-title">Hash Functions</p>
        <p class="gl-card-desc">How HMAC and SHA-256 power JWT signature verification.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/guides/json-formatter-guide.html" class="gl-card">
        <span class="gl-card-icon">💻</span>
        <p class="gl-card-title">JSON Formatter Guide</p>
        <p class="gl-card-desc">Clean up decoded payloads and fix syntax errors fast.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</GuideLayout>
